From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): CORRECTION - two independent KV defects, not
 one head_dim story

The previous entry concluded "quantized KV + FA is broken at head_dim 128". That
was wrong. All the head_dim 256 evidence had been taken on the promoted llama.cpp
runtime, never on PrismML's own build. Running the pristine PrismML build (build 1,
commit 9a9394a, no TurboQuant code) on SC117 (head_dim 256):

  f16 6.9921    q8_0 92.2627    q4_0 7.0140

q8_0 KV is broken on PrismML's base at every head size - 329.4764 at 128 and
92.2627 at 256 - so the 329 in the earlier table was never a head_dim effect. It
just happened to sit next to a real one.

Two independent defects:

  A. PrismML's base breaks q8_0 KV at any head size. Reproduces on the pristine
     build, q4_0 is fine, and their own KV work is scoped to Q4_0 by construction
     (the mean-centering feature rejects any other K type). Their 93 own commits
     touched no FA file at all.

  B. TurboQuant KV breaks at head_dim 128 (8038.7921) and is fine at 256 (7.1292),
     on both branches, with q8_0 as a working control on the llama.cpp base.

The cheap test that would have separated them - PrismML's own build with q8_0 KV on
a head_dim 256 model - was skipped because those numbers already existed on the
other runtime. Cross-runtime comparisons need the same control run on both.

Also recorded: test-backend-ops on this build reports FLASH_ATTN_EXT failures
clustered at hsk=72 (the non-128 padding gap the port map already tracks) and ZERO
at hsk=128, so the attention kernel is numerically right at 128 and defect B is at
the graph / cache level rather than in the kernel.
